,"detail":"json.loads raises RecursionError, a RuntimeError, on input such as b'[' * 40000, which fits under MAX_INVENTORY_BYTES with exit code 0. _parse_packages only converts UnicodeDecodeError and ValueError, and list_image_packages catches only OSError, ValueError and SubprocessError, so the exception escapes through image_packages and contract_context and the context or review run command fails with a traceback. Nothing is cached, so every later context call starts another container and fails again, contradicting the documented unavailable entry and one-container-per-run behaviour.","fix_commit":"1951839318f21e5643c43c70060ef6ea3c2aed13","id":"F001","line":312,"path":"agentic_preflight/contract_runner.py","response_note":null,"severity":"medium","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Catch RecursionError in _parse_packages alongside the JSON errors and raise the same ValueError so the listing becomes an unavailable entry that is cached.","title":"Deeply nested listing output crashes context instead of yielding unavailable","unit":"U0009"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"_read_inventory catches only OSError and ValueError. A contracts/images/<digest>.json under the 1 MiB cap that consists of nested brackets raises RecursionError out of json.loads, so the reader's 'derived again' fallback does not hold and context fails on every call.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F002","line":142,"path":"agentic_preflight/runs/contracts.py","response_note":"Repaired in commit 1951839 together with F001; that commit is the snapshot the clean review covers. Recorded as a note because the CLI refuses a fix commit that predates the resubmission.","severity":"medium","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Add RecursionError to the except clause so a corrupt cache entry is re-derived.","title":"Cache reader does not survive a deeply nested cache file","unit":"U0013"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"test_real_image_listing_runs_unprivileged_and_offline asserts only availability, a non-empty package list, cleanup success and container removal. Nothing inspects the user or the network; those flags are covered by the fake-engine argv test.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F003","line":805,"path":"tests/test_contract_checks.py","response_note":"Repaired in commit 1951839 together with F001; that commit is the snapshot the clean review covers. Recorded as a note because the CLI refuses a fix commit that predates the resubmission.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Rename the test to describe what it checks, for example test_real_image_listing_returns_packages_and_removes_its_container.","title":"Integration test name claims unprivileged and offline properties it does not assert","unit":"U0026"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"test_unavailable_listing_is_explicit_and_never_host_run asserts the unavailable entry, its reason, caching and the recorded engine calls. A direct host subprocess would not be observed by the faked _capture, so the 'never host run' claim is not exercised.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F004","line":449,"path":"tests/test_contract_checks.py","response_note":"Repaired in commit 1951839 together with F001; that commit is the snapshot the clean review covers. Recorded as a note because the CLI refuses a fix commit that predates the resubmission.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Rename to test_unavailable_listing_is_explicit_with_a_reason.","title":"Test name claims never host run without asserting it","unit":"U0024"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"contract_context removes plan_schema only after a schema-2 receipt is found. With a legacy schema-1 receipt it returns previous_receipt together with plan_schema, so 'until a receipt exists' is wrong for that case.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F005","line":154,"path":"skill/reference/commands.md","response_note":"Repaired in commit 1951839 together wit